# The text display trap (reference/TEXT_DISPLAYS.md): a long text that changes every second never shows its end,
# because the game keeps the scroll position on every change and clamps it back. Keep the changing value short
# (about 7 characters) and put the caption on a display of its own. The run passes when the sandbox catches the
# long one and stays quiet about the short one.
name text display: long changing text vs short value + caption
dev bad display
dev caption display
dev good display

box meter
note "A FAKE REACTOR METER" "A 1 Hz pulse counts up from 1000 kW. out1 = the long text (unreadable), out2 = the short value (fine)."
c tick osc OutputType=Pulse Frequency=1
c n mem Value=1000
c inc add
w n.out inc.1 short.1 long.2
w tick.out inc.2
w inc.out n.in
c head mem Value="Reactor output:"
c unit mem Value=kW
c long concat Separator=" "
c long2 concat Separator=" "
w head.out long.1
w long.out long2.1
w unit.out long2.2 short.2
w long2.out out1
c short concat Separator=" "
w short.out out2
c cap mem Value=OUTPUT
w cap.out out3

wire meter.out1 bad.set_text
wire meter.out2 good.set_text
wire meter.out3 caption.set_text

expectwarn display bad: .*snaps the scroll back
expect 20 good ~ ^10[0-9][0-9] kW$
expect 20 caption = OUTPUT
run 30
